---
import { DOCS_URL } from "../config/distribution";

const steps = [
  { command: "vario init", comment: "connect ClickHouse, choose sources" },
  { command: "vario run", comment: "start collecting" },
];
---

<section
  aria-labelledby="start-title"
  class="shell grid grid-cols-1 gap-x-10 gap-y-10 py-[clamp(6rem,14vw,10rem)] md:grid-cols-12 md:items-baseline"
>
  <div class="md:col-span-5">
    <h2
      id="start-title"
      class="text-[clamp(2.25rem,5.2vw,4rem)] leading-none font-medium tracking-[-0.045em] text-ink"
    >
      Get started
    </h2>
  </div>

  <div class="max-w-[34rem] md:col-span-7">
    <pre class="overflow-x-auto text-[0.9375rem] leading-[2] sm:text-base">{
        steps.map((step) => (
          <code class="block whitespace-pre"><span class="text-accent select-none" aria-hidden="true">$ </span><span class="text-ink">{step.command.padEnd(12)}</span><span class="hidden text-faint select-none sm:inline"># {step.comment}</span></code>
        ))
      }</pre>

    <p class="mt-8 leading-relaxed text-pretty text-muted">
      <code class="code">init</code> walks you through the setup: connecting to
      ClickHouse, creating the database, choosing what to collect and selecting
      your sources. <code class="code">run</code> then collects continuously.
      Background services, migrations and queries are covered in the{" "}
      <a class="link" href={DOCS_URL}>
        documentation
      </a>
      .
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
